dd9|n|A large, closed, four-wheeled carriage, having doors in the sides, and generally a front and back seat inside, each for two persons, and an elevated outside seat in front for the driver. ; A special tutor who assists in preparing a student for examination; a trainer; esp. one who trains a boat's crew for a race. ; A cabin on the after part of the quarter-deck, usually occupied by the captain. ; A first-class passenger car, as distinguished from a drawing-room car, sleeping car, etc. It is sometimes loosely applied to any passenger car.	a:599,105,2;51h,55,3;x0g,40,1~51h,55,3;599,105,2;x0g,40,1	v:asx,46,3;29d3,38,3~29d3,38,3;asx,46,3	n:smb,111,5;163a,58,5;x0g,40,1;asx,40,2;29d3,22,1~163a,58,5;smb,111,5;asx,40,2;29d3,22,1;x0g,40,1
