e6e|n|The act of comparing; an examination of two or more objects with the view of discovering the resemblances or differences; relative estimate. ; The state of being compared; a relative estimate; also, a state, quality, or relation, admitting of being compared; as, to bring a thing into comparison with another; there is no comparison between them. ; That to which, or with which, a thing is compared, as being equal or like; illustration; similitude. ; The modification, by inflection or otherwise, which the adjective and adverb undergo to denote degrees of quality or quantity; as, little, less, least, are examples of comparison. ; A figure by which one person or thing is compared to another, or the two are considered with regard to some property or quality, which is common to them both; e.g., the lake sparkled like a jewel. ; The faculty of the reflective group which is supposed to perceive resemblances and contrasts.	a:1nei,53,4;220u,47,2;kcb,46,11;26le,32,3;qfc,32,2;qw1,29,4;25cl,26,1;1vto,24,3;12g0,22,4;1m36,21,2~kcb,46,11;ugg,17,5;1z4b,4,4;12g0,22,4;qw1,29,4;1nei,53,4;1p9l,16,3;1vto,24,3;7ey,0,3;26le,32,3	v:12g0,2,1~12g0,2,1	n:1hlu,41,5;220u,37,1;25cl,36,2;m4,32,2;1wkt,32,5;1m36,11,1;224y,9,4~1hlu,41,5;1wkt,32,5;224y,9,4;25cl,36,2;m4,32,2;220u,37,1;1m36,11,1	N:20gx,58,6;22p9,39,5;vzb,22,5;21hb,5,1;htb,2,2~20gx,58,6;22p9,39,5;vzb,22,5;htb,2,2;21hb,5,1
